  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Keep the deterministic snapshot in the default snapshot prompt when an active user intent/question is present, instead of replacing the snapshot with the intent.\n- Preserve provider/model identity, context-window settings, prompt-cache capabilities, and post-call usage/cache sidecars across the symbiosis metering wrappers.\n- Clarify cache-ghost wording so it matches the implemented/provider physics: Mantle appends only the semantic delta internally, while real prompt-cache transports still present the accumulated byte-stable prefix so cached prefill can reduce metabolic cost.\n- Add focused regression coverage for snapshot+intent assembly and cache-capable metered transports.\n\n## Why\n\nMantle's metabolic model depends on provider prompt caching. The Body should append experiential deltas internally while the MIND transport presents the full accumulated context for prefix-cache reuse. Two runtime seams undermined that contract: snapshot mode could drop assembled context when a question was supplied, and symbiosis metering hid the underlying transport's cache capabilities and receipts. The Ghost prose also described delta-only wire transmission even though the implementation correctly recognizes that real prompt caches reuse compute rather than eliminating the prefix from the request.\n\n## Scope\n\nSurgical only. Rolling-prefix construction, VCW authority, containment, cache policy, and provider-neutral transport semantics are unchanged. No stateful-continuation redesign is introduced.\n\n## Validation\n\nFocused tests were added/updated. This execution environment cannot clone GitHub or run the repository locally, so the repository's GitHub Actions checks are the executable validation for this branch.",
